---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Pragmatic AI for Regulated Industries"
	description="AI strategy, governance, and private AI for regulated businesses — governance first, then the workflows where AI delivers measurable benefit."
>
	<Nav />

	<!-- Hero -->
	<section class="hero">
		<p class="hero-eyebrow">AI Strategy · Governance · Private AI</p>
		<h1>Pragmatic AI for regulated industries.</h1>
		<p class="hero-subhead">
			Most organizations have seen the promise of AI. Fewer have seen it work inside their compliance obligations.
			Ohana Tech helps regulated businesses decide where AI earns its place, govern it from day one,
			and run it on infrastructure they control.
		</p>
		<div class="hero-ctas">
			<a href="/services" class="btn btn-primary">Our Services</a>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Start a Conversation</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider" />

	<!-- What we do -->
	<section class="section">
		<p class="section-label">What we do</p>
		<h2>Governance first, then where AI pays off.</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">
			In a regulated business, the hardest questions about AI are rarely about the model. They're about
			accountability, data boundaries, and whether the result will hold up in an audit. We start there,
			then help you find the workflows where AI delivers measurable benefit.
		</p>
		<div class="service-grid">
			<div class="service-card">
				<h3>AI Strategy & Governance</h3>
				<p>
					An assessment of where AI fits in your business, an AI use policy your people can follow, and a
					phased roadmap tied to the controls your regulators and customers already expect.
				</p>
				<a href="/services#strategy" class="service-card-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
			</div>
			<div class="service-card">
				<h3>Private AI</h3>
				<p>
					AI that runs inside your security boundary on open-weight models, with governance built in and
					capacity-based costs you can forecast. Your data stays with you, and you aren't tied to one
					vendor's pricing cycle.
				</p>
				<a href="/services#private-ai" class="service-card-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
			</div>
			<div class="service-card">
				<h3>Implementation</h3>
				<p>
					Pilots and production rollout that follow the roadmap: integration with your existing systems,
					access controls, audit trails, and training so adoption keeps pace with governance.
				</p>
				<a href="/services#implementation" class="service-card-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider" />

	<!-- Clients -->
	<section class="section">
		<p class="section-label">Who we work with</p>
		<h2>Regulated businesses where the details matter.</h2>
		<ul class="highlight-list">
			<li>
				<strong>Nextern</strong>
				ISO 13485-certified medical device contract development and manufacturing organization, White Bear Lake, MN.
				Integrating AI-assisted development into regulated engineering workflows under IEC 62304 and FDA 21 CFR 820.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Everest Business Funding</strong>
				Miami-based provider of revenue-based financing for small and midsize businesses. AI discovery and a
				governance framework spanning underwriting, sales, servicing, and operations.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider" />

	<!-- Experience -->
	<section class="section">
		<p class="section-label">Experience</p>
		<h2>Decades inside regulated technology.</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">
			Our work draws on long experience building and running technology where compliance, safety, and
			reliability are part of the job.
		</p>
		<ul class="highlight-list">
			<li>
				<strong>Optum / UnitedHealth Group — 8 years</strong>
				Technology executive for advanced clinical solutions. Designed and built Calypso, a multi-EHR integration
				platform on FHIR and SMART on FHIR. Led Optum's technical engagement on 21st Century Cures compliance.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Red Hat</strong>
				Architect for embedded systems, OpenStack, and OpenShift — the cloud-native infrastructure that now runs
				AI workloads in production.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>IBM — Software Development Product Management</strong>
				Product management across IBM's software portfolio. Conceived and drove the open sourcing of Eclipse.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>U.S. Navy</strong>
				Naval service, followed by program management for shipbuilding with the Department of the Navy.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
			<a href="/about" class="btn btn-secondary">Full background &rarr;</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider" />

	<!-- Governance callout -->
	<section class="section">
		<p class="section-label">Why governance comes first</p>
		<h2>Frameworks are written for people. AI acts on data.</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">
			Regulations and frameworks such as NIST AI RMF, the EU AI Act, and industry quality standards are written
			in natural language for human reviewers. AI systems act on structured data and explicit constraints.
			Much of the difficulty in regulated AI deployment lives in the space between the two.
		</p>
		<p class="section-intro">
			Ohana developed the open Structured Context Specification to close that gap, so governance requirements
			reach AI systems in a form they can use and auditors can check.
		</p>
		<p>
			<a href="https://structuredcontext.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-secondary">
				Structured Context Specification &rarr;
			</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- CTA banner -->
	<div class="cta-banner">
		<div class="cta-banner-inner">
			<div>
				<h2>Have a use case in mind?</h2>
				<p>Most engagements start with a focused conversation about one problem. We'll tell you plainly whether AI is the right answer.</p>
			</div>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
		</div>
	</div>

	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
